{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.Mass.DeuteronBindingDressing","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.Mass.DeuteronBindingDressing","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Real.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Ring","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.FieldSimp","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith","lean:module:QOU.ParticleInteractions.neutron_qvalue_symbolic"],"declarations":3,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.binding_dressing_eq_qbeta_over_h","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.binding_dressing_eq_qbeta_over_h","kind":"theorem","line":70,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeuteronBindingDressing.lean#L70-L83","doc":"**The deuteron binding dressing is the proton NF net coefficient.**\nThe candidate binding functional `E₀ · net(p) · Δtr` equals the\n`Q_β`-scaled trace difference `Q_β · Δtr / h` for any `Δtr`, i.e. the\n`(1 − h/2)` dressing on the `E₀` route is exactly `net(p)`, the\nbar-even partner of `Q_β` under the single Hecke factor `h`. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:deuteron-binding-dressing-proton-net","label":"prop:deuteron-binding-dressing-proton-net","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/deuteron-binding-dressing-proton-net.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.qbeta_eq_E0_h_net_p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.qbeta_eq_E0_h_net_p","kind":"theorem","line":53,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeuteronBindingDressing.lean#L53-L68","doc":"**`Q_β = E₀ · h · net(p)`.**  Substituting `|Δ(net)| = h · net(p)`\n(from `delta_net_eq_neg_h_net_p` and `0 < h < 2`) into the `Q`-value\nansatz gives the `Q`-value as `E₀` times `h · net(p)`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.Mass.delta_net_eq_neg_h_net_p","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.Mass.delta_net_eq_neg_h_net_p","kind":"theorem","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/Mass/DeuteronBindingDressing.lean#L45-L51","doc":"**`Δ(net) = −h · net(p)` (division-free).**  The neutron−proton NF net\ndifference is exactly `−h` times the proton NF net coefficient — the\nidentity that ties the deuteron binding dressing to the `Q`-value. ","signatureChunk":0}]}